Subject: [#94-2-66] Is this a bug?

At about 1045 PST Sunday 6 February, I sent a two-line message to
extropians@extropy.org.  The "To:" and "Subject:" lines as they appeared on
my console prior to transmission, and the body, were as follows:
 
    To: extropians@extropy.org
    Subject: Re:  Extropians List Statistics 1/30

    An interesting addition to the weekly Extropians List Statistics might be
    the total number of list members.                         --  Jay Freeman

Within half an hour I received the following from extropians-request:

    To: freeman@cleo
    From: extropians-request@extropy.org (List Processing System)
    Subject: Error: Message Not Sent, empty or short message

    An interesting addition to the weekly Extropians List Statistics might be
    the total number of list members.                         --  Jay Freeman

Obviously, the message was not received empty, since the List Processing
System was able to send back a copy of the body.  And I had thought that
brevity of posting was a virtue -- if not, I suppose I could be considerably
more verbose -- let me see, where did I put those old Detweiler postings from
cypherpunks, they'd be good padding...

Seriously, I trust that our standards of composition have not sunk so low that
a short message is automatically taken to be an inconsequential one.

                                    -- Jay Freeman, Squirrel of Few Words

